Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff-x86_64.c
Line: 647
Function: coff_pe_amd64_relocate_section
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-787
Explanation: Writes a 16-bit value to contents + (rel->r_vaddr - input_section->vma) without validating that r_vaddr lies within the input section’s contents. A crafted object can set r_vaddr outside the section, causing an out-of-bounds write (or underflow leading to a large positive offset).

